WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.360
Thanksgiving Day gives us a chance to share
a meal with family and friends.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.620
It also offers a time to reflect upon those
who are less fortunate and the things we can

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.779
do to make sure no child goes hungry in this
country.

00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:23.100
In 2018 alone, Americans gave more than
$50 billion to organizations like food pantries,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.169
homeless shelters, and soup kitchens.

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:29.540
Nearly a third of charitable giving occurs
during the holidays, and helping to feed the

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.030
hungry is a top volunteer activity for Americans.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:39.969
The federal government plays a role too. It spent
close to $100 billion in 2018 on programs

00:00:39.969 --> 00:00:44.940
like SNAP, school lunches, and nutritional
assistance for new moms and infants.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:50.700
Thanks to these efforts, fewer than one percent
of children in 2018 reduced their food intake

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.140
because of a lack of money.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.840
Good nutrition is essential for child
development and human flourishing.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:00.809
On this day and throughout the year, it is
important to remember our shared responsibility

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:06.159
as a society, not just the government, to
make sure that child hunger in this country

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:07.440
remains rare.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.220
How do you plan to help the needy this Thanksgiving?

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:11.840
Let us know on our poll.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:17.080
Also let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:21.540
and be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

